    "result_text": "BUILD SUCCESS \u2014 all 3 tests pass (the only test class in the suite).\n\n## Summary\n\nTelephone numbers are now stored and returned in E.164 form, with duplicate detection comparing E.164 values. Changes:\n\n1. **`E164Telephone.java`** (new, package-private helper) \u2014 one small static `toE164` method: strips non-digits (spaces/dashes/brackets); if there's a leading `+`, keeps the country code as-is; otherwise assumes `+61` and drops a single leading `0`; returns `null` unless the result has 8\u201315 digits after `+`. Shared so the two callers hold no duplicated logic.\n\n2. **`NormalizeOwnerTelephone.java`** \u2014 its one method now calls `E164Telephone.toE164` and rejects with 400 (`MissingOwnerFieldsException`) when it returns `null`, replacing the old exactly-10-digits rule.\n\n3. **`RejectDuplicateOwnerTelephone.java`** \u2014 compares the owner's E.164 telephone against each other owner's E.164 form (deleted its old digits-only `normalize` helper).\n\n4. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 relaxed the `telephone` bean-validation constraint from `^[0-9]{10}$` / `@Digits(integer=10)` to `^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$` so the stored E.164 value passes JPA persist validation.\n\n**Structural impact:** each changed method stays tiny and sits in a tiny class (each function file holds one function, so `WMC_other \u2248 0`). The new logic lives in its own cohesive unit rather than growing an existing method. The `Owner` edit touched only field annotations, not any method body. No endpoint YAML, DTO, or mapper changes were needed \u2014 POST binds `@RequestBody` without `@Valid`, so validation happens where the pipeline explicitly does it.",
